sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as UI / CAN command
    participant Control as PlayerController
    participant Life as MediaSessionLifecycle
    participant Gate as PlaybackCoordinator
    participant Media as MediaPlayer / VideoOutput
    Note over User,Media: Logical ordering on main, not a measured time scale
    User->>Control: Next / Previous / select another track
    Control->>Gate: stopRequested, cancel pending Play
    Control->>Life: stopRequested, reset generation
    Life->>Media: Stop, clear source, release session
    Control->>Life: sourceChanged, update desiredSource and reset generation
    Control->>Gate: playRequested, record pending Play and current source
    Note over Life,Gate: C++ queued work runs after the current callback, not after a fixed delay
    Note over Gate: Pause / Stop / source replacement cancels pending Play and invalidates old tickets
    Life->>Life: Reject obsolete generation tickets
    Life->>Media: Create session, attach VideoOutput, then assign source
    Media-->>Gate: Ready when media reaches a supported state
    Gate->>Gate: Queued C++ callback, recheck generation and source
    Gate->>Media: Play
    Media-->>Gate: Playing, clear pending Play
    Media-->>Control: Report playback, position and duration
    Media-->>Gate: EndOfMedia
    Gate->>Gate: Queued C++ callback, confirm the source is still current
    Gate->>Control: handleEndOfMedia
    alt Auto Next enabled
        Control->>Control: Select next track and repeat source-switch sequence
    else Auto Next disabled
        Control->>Control: Set finished, retain session and final frame
    end
